{{!--
  THE BAG BAR (08 §11's *You wear up to four containers at once*; D-736).

  WoW's own strip of bag icons, in three runs:

  - the **four general places**, and the counted ones beside them — one
    quiver, one bolt case, one powder horn, one bandolier, one scroll case;
  - the **one mount or vehicle** that is with you, which adds its own wells
    by its **Carries** figure (08 §15);
  - the **Stable**, where every other mount and vehicle stands. A stabled
    mount adds nothing and is carried by nobody, so it takes no bag slot and
    it is still drawn, because nothing is ever hidden.

  An EMPTY place is a drop zone and nothing else: `data-bag-zone` says what a
  drop there means, and the place itself carries no `data-action`, so a click
  on furniture does nothing rather than something surprising. A FILLED place
  is an ordinary tile carrying its own `data-container-id`, so a thing dropped
  on the icon goes in that bag and a CONTAINER takes its place.

  **THE ZONE IS THE RUN, not the list of places inside it** (the lead,
  2026-09-20: *I'm unable to drag a mount into the slot*). The box a reader
  sees and aims at is `.azeroth-bag-bar-run` - its heading, its six pixels of
  padding and the wells within them - and while the attribute sat on the
  `<ol>` a drop on the word *Mount*, or anywhere in the padding, matched no
  zone at all: `_onDropItem` handed the event back to core and the mount was
  left exactly where it was. Every test aimed at the `<ol>` and so could not
  see it. Whatever lights on a dragover is `zone.el`, so moving the attribute
  moves the outline onto the same box.
--}}
<div class="azeroth-bag-bar">
  <div class="azeroth-bag-bar-run" data-bag-zone="bar">
    <h4 class="azeroth-bag-bar-head">{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.Worn"}}</h4>
    <ol class="azeroth-bag-places" role="listbox" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.Worn"}}">
      {{#each bags.bar as |place|}}
      {{#if place.tile}}
      {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/bag-tile.hbs tile=place.tile}}
      {{else}}
      <li class="azeroth-bag-well is-empty is-place" data-tooltip="{{place.hint}}" aria-label="{{place.hint}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></li>
      {{/if}}
      {{/each}}
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="azeroth-bag-bar-run" data-bag-zone="mount">
    <h4 class="azeroth-bag-bar-head">{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.Mount"}}</h4>
    <ol class="azeroth-bag-places" role="listbox" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.Mount"}}">
      {{#if bags.mount}}
      {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/bag-tile.hbs tile=bags.mount}}
      {{else}}
      <li class="azeroth-bag-well is-empty is-place" data-tooltip="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.EmptyMount"}}" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.EmptyMount"}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></li>
      {{/if}}
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="azeroth-bag-bar-run azeroth-bag-bar-stable" data-bag-zone="stable">
    <h4 class="azeroth-bag-bar-head">{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.Stable"}}</h4>
    <ol class="azeroth-bag-places" role="listbox" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.Stable"}}">
      {{#each bags.stable as |tile|}}
      {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/bag-tile.hbs tile=tile}}
      {{else}}
      <li class="azeroth-bag-well is-empty is-place" data-tooltip="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.EmptyStable"}}" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Bags.EmptyStable"}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-horse" aria-hidden="true"></i></li>
      {{/each}}
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>
